            <ArticleTitle>17-year-old runner with shin pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>238-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2967/jnmt.113.135897</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Stress injury is a common cause of exercise-induced anterior shin pain. It is important to distinguish between the various causes of stress injury in a timely manner in order to optimize favorable treatment outcomes. Here, we will discuss a case of medial tibial stress syndrome, or shin splints, as one of the causes of shin pain, as well as how to approach shin pain for a successful diagnosis.</AbstractText>
